      "content": "This study elucidates the mechanistic role of ionizable cationic lipids with physiological pKa values (6.2–6.5) in facilitating state-dependent conformational changes within the multilamellar structure of late endosomes. The optimized cationic lipid interactively disrupts the protonated membrane integrity through electrophoretic destabilization, enabling efficient cargo release into the cytosol. Simultaneously, the precise molar integration of PEGylated chains modulates surface hydrodynamic radius and electrostatic zeta potential, which governs systemic circulation half-life and reduces non-specific uptake by reticuloendothelial organs. Consequently, fine-tuning the lipid-to-nucleic acid ratio minimizes off-target activation of toll-like receptors and downstream cytokine storms, while maximizing translational protein output within hepatocytes. This approach provides a rational design framework for next-generation mRNA therapeutics requiring robust endosomal escape vectors.",
